// @name: Superposition — group + per-note cutoff
// @tagline: two filters in series on one param
// @description: SUPERP-1 test scene: a slow GROUP cutoff envelope (a shared bus over the whole phrase) and a fast PER-NOTE cutoff envelope superpose in series on the same parameter. Each note re-triggers its own filter, then passes through the group bus.
// @language: bpscript
// @outputs: audio
// @level: advanced
// @tags: cv, modulation, superposition, test
//
// SUPERP-1 test scene — a GROUP cutoff filter and a PER-NOTE cutoff filter on the
// SAME parameter, superposed in SERIES. The {…} GROUP carries the slow group cutoff
// envelope (a shared bus over the whole sequential group); each note inside also
// re-triggers a fast PER-NOTE cutoff envelope (*:cutoff). Note → per-note filter →
// group bus → output. Proof: the two superpose, the group filter's phase varies with
// the note's position in the group, and a fresh bus is keyed per loop occurrence.

@core
@controls
@alphabet.western:browser
@tempo:96

cv envGroup : mod.adsr(attack:600, decay:500, sustain:0.5, release:700)
cv envNote  : mod.adsr(attack:5, decay:110, sustain:0.2, release:160)

S -> { Phrase }(cutoff:envGroup)
Phrase -> C2 C3 C2 C3 (*:cutoff:envNote, wave:sawtooth, vel:100, filterQ:8)
